  "findings": [
    "All eighteen complete lock-record before/after transitions and each frozen metadata package ID, selected declaration fields, manifest features and full resolve node equal the independently read original Cargo proposal.",
    "Registry transitions reject duplicate identities, empty transitions, non-dependency metadata changes, missing or extra dependency entries, and an incomplete applied inventory. Other registry/Git package changes remain rejected.",
    "Metadata compares unique package identities and IDs with the generated lock and requires an exact one-to-one resolver-node inventory. Each reviewed registry node is compared in full, including feature activation, dependency kinds and targets.",
    "All ten original control function bodies remain byte-identical; only their fixture CONFIG gains the two empty transition fields. Twenty new methods yield thirty controls to execute.",
    "Original formatter, Cargo metadata, Bazel lock-update/check command sequence and qualification requiring first lock-check success and an unchanged checkout remain unchanged.",
    "The local-package allowlist adds only codex-hepta-fleet. Formatter scope adds twenty-eight source/configuration paths; none are removed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The static review did not execute Python parsing, the thirty controls, Cargo resolution or any product/native gate.",
    "metadata_document is a parser for one compact Cargo metadata v1 JSON line surrounded by diagnostics; it is not a general-purpose validator of arbitrary JSON streams.",
    "Full resolver nodes are independently frozen only for the eighteen reviewed registry records. Local-package dependency changes remain governed by the existing package-name allowlist and must be reviewed in the actual generated delta.",
    "Correctness and security of the newly composed product sources are outside this generation-boundary review. Generated-needs-adoption is not a qualified unchanged source."
  ],
